d content. Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : IndexedDB VISITOR_INFO1_LIVE Tries to estimate the users' bandwidth on pages with integrated YouTube videos. Maximum Storage Duration : 180 days Type : HTTP Cookie YSC Registers a unique ID to keep statistics of what videos from YouTube the user has seen. Maximum Storage Duration : Session Type : HTTP Cookie Unclassified 7 Unclassified cookies are cookies that we are in the process of classifying, together with the providers of individual cookies. LinkedIn 1 Learn more about this provider li_fat_id Pending Maximum Storage Duration : 30 days Type : HTTP Cookie Tu/e 3 Learn more about this provider aff_2577a2901 Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Session Type : HTTP Cookie aff_93e95bd6a Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Session Type : HTTP Cookie page_view_count Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Session Type : HTML Local Storage YouTube 3 Learn more about this provider PersistentEntityStoreDb:V34421bd5||#EntityAssociationStore Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : IndexedDB PersistentEntityStoreDb:V34421bd5||#EntityStore Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : IndexedDB yt-player-caption-persistence Pending Maximum Storage Duration : Persistent Type : HTML Local Storage Cross-domain consent [#BULK_CONSENT_DOMAINS_COUNT#] [#BULK_CONSENT_TITLE#] List of domains your consent applies to: [#BULK_CONSENT_DOMAINS#] Cookie declaration last updated on 8/27/26 by Cookiebot [#IABV2_TITLE#] [#IABV2_BODY_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_LEGITIMATE_INTEREST_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PREFERENCE_INTRO#] [#IABV2_LABEL_PURPOSES#] [#IABV2_BODY_PURPOSES_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PURPOSES#] [#IABV2_LABEL_FEATURES#] [#IABV2_BODY_FEATURES_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_FEATURES#] [#IABV2_LABEL_PARTNERS#] [#IABV2_BODY_PARTNERS_INTRO#] [#IABV2_BODY_PARTNERS#] About Cookies are small text files that can be used by websites to make a user's experience more efficient. The law states that we can store cookies on your device if they are strictly necessary for the operation of this site. For all other types of cookies we need your permission. This website uses different types of cookies. Some cookies are placed by third party services that appear on our pages. You can at any time change or withdraw your consent from the cookie declaration on our website. Please state your consent ID and date when you contact us regarding your consent. For more information about the use of cookies at TU/e you can visit: https://www.tue.nl/en/storage/disclaimer Do not sell or share my personal information Deny Allow selection Customize Allow all Skip to content Menu Close the menu Menu Eindhoven University of Technology Education Research Our university Working at TU/e News and Events Impact × search Search Nederlands NL Search Working at TU/e Vacancies Scientific Staff Scientific Staff Academic Perspectives Irène Curie Program Learning & Development Personal Grants Partner Career Support Program Scientific Staff Vacancies Support Staff Support Staff Learning & Development Support Staff Vacancies PhD EngD At TU/e Why TU/e Conditions of Employment Application Process Support for Internationals Home Working at TU/e Vacancies Education IT Consult... Working at TU/e Directly to Create job alert Login to (re)view your application(s) Login as an employee to view internal vacancies Education IT Consultant (1 FTE) Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: IT Organisation: Department of Mathematics and Computer Science Apply no later than: 28-09-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 6.682 Apply now Introduction Are you an IT enthusiast who wants to rise above yourself, in both your profession and as a person? At the TU/e, scientists and students continuously create the unthinkable. The strength of TU/e’s IT landscape is their key to success and, hence, so are you as being an essential contributor to that landscape. These creative minds expect you to offer them a solution for tomorrow that doesn’t exist today. Together we are building the high - performance backbone that this epicenter of science and technology demands. Are you driven by taking ownership and do you have an entrepreneurial mindset? We like to get in touch with you! Job Description As an education IT consultant, you work in collaboration with teaching and support staff to develop sustainable IT products, services and workflows. You have a leading implementation role in setting up what is needed to reach this goal. You are in the proximity of the department and its IT landscape, and you are part of a multidisciplinary team in which you share and learn from each other’s knowledge and expertise. You work for a department which fosters diverse education and innovation, requiring highly specialized technology. With your broad range of interests, expertise and ability to oversee the complex landscape of interests and challenges, you’re enabled to take the lead on what’s needed, so that the teachers can focus on their most innovative work. You will also have the opportunity to build up an extensive network and to specialize in relevant educational areas. In this role, you will contribute to the ambition of the Beethoven program to educate top talent and strengthen research across the fields of Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics (STEM). Functionally, you report to the IT business owner of M&CS. How this looks like in practice? Read the following section for an impression: A typical week of an Education IT consultant at M&CS On Monday, you start the week together with your team of experts (“The Hub”), and review the current developments and your activities at M&CS. Together with the IT business owner, you align on priorities, discuss impediments and determine tactics for the best approach. In the afternoon, you visit a teacher who wants to provide their students sufficient compute resources and is looking for efficient allocation. You advise them on what resources could be suitable for this use case and optionally get them in contact with expert support on this topic. At the same time, you notice you receive this type of questions quite often, so you coordinate with the back-office to make sure we can support this type of requests in a sustainable way for the future. On Tuesday, you work out a plan to facilitate in the IT requirements for an upcoming course, in alignment with the TU/e policies and frameworks. In particular, the exams need guidance and support in enabling a robust digital assessment process. In the afternoon, you investigate how students can easily access APIs for LLMs and what type of procedures ensures a responsible disclosure of them. As other scientific departments also might want to learn about this, you navigate through your network to offer your services proactively. On Wednesday, you work at home and focus on developing and testing the various options for a configuration to enable student groups to operate a number of machines. You do this in collaboration with your expert colleague who knows all the relevant technical aspects. You maintain a close feedback loop with the teaching organization and make agreements on structural support of the prototype. In the afternoon, you receive a funding proposal for an innovative approach in education, and you advice in the feasibility of integration and the border conditions for implementation. On Thursday, you meet the management during your regular check-in moment to report on the progress. Their ambition is to embed sustainable IT solutions in the department’s education, especially in the light of the growth of Beethoven. You have prepared your ideas in advance, based on input of your stakeholders (e.g., teaching staff of M&CS, the Educational Management Team, TU/e’s IT department LIS, TU/e’s education service department ESA), your current overview, user data and openings for improvements. Some actions are needed, for instance, some of the deployed products suffer from bus factor = 1, so it’s important that ICT strategy and implementation are aligned for any further measures. Fully equipped with support, you set out actions to lead the change. On Friday, you work on an often mentioned frustration point of submitting grades in multiple systems and you analyze how to streamline this process better. Also you received a request to consult on a data management workflow how to handle digital exam data given the obligations within the accredited courses. You have a call with education advisors in the afternoon to work out the details and you contribute to the technical aspects of the workflow. Responsibilities and core tasks Acquiring projects that contribute to supporting teaching staff of M&CS in their IT needs; Coordinating broader educational IT demand and (new) initiatives to sustainable solutions; Integrating (the functionalities of) existing educational tooling in courses and streamlining existing digital processes in collaboration with the relevant team(s); Hardening of the current education IT landscape (e.g., robust capacity, security and privacy aspects, product support); Helping teachers how to use IT in a responsible and effective way; M&CS-specific ambitions integration in the education IT landscape (e.g., explore ways of digitization of courses, how AI can reduce workload, developing BI insights, contribute to professionalizing in-house developed products) Perform stakeholder management while working with financial limitations and existing organizational frameworks; Your impact extends beyond technology, it’s about empowering people and driving excellence. Job Requirements You have a minimum education of a Master’s degree or PhD degree, preferably with a background in Computer Science, Data Science or any related field; Years of experience in higher education. You are able to effectively communicate with scientific staff. You empathize well with what moves the teaching staff and their primary processes; You are organizationally sensitive and service-oriented; you initiate and maintain relevant relationships with customers, (key) user groups, and suppliers; You have strong affinity, experience or expertise on what makes IT sustainable (e.g., secure, scalable fit-for-purpose); You are a pleasant collaboration partner and team player for both scientists and the IT back office, thereby mediating between organization and innovation; You initiate action to innovate existing products and services, based on the interest of the department you represent and you can operate independently within constraints of time and resources; You have experience with one or more of the following techniques: Remote computing (cloud and / or on premise), Research Data Management and processing, Software Engineering, Git and / or code repository management, Software Licensing, AI related topics, Internet of Things, Infrastructural Architecture; Experience with scripting and automating workflows, in particular in Linux OS, is a bonus; Strongly developed process- and project-oriented thinking; Excellent proficiency (speaking and writing) in English, and preferably Dutch. If you are concerned that you don’t meet all the requirements sufficiently, but the job does excite you, then be sure to respond, we would love to look at your profile. Conditions of Employment An exciting position within an international yet personal university. You are right in the middle of the students, on a green campus within walking distance of the central station. Besides beautiful architecture, you will find varied workplaces and excellent sports facilities. We also offer you: Salary in accordance with the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities , scale 11, ranging from € 4,925 to € 6,682 gross base salary per month (full-time), depending on your knowledge and experience. In addition to your base salary, you will receive an 8% holiday allowance and an 8.3% year-end bonus, both calculated based on your annual gross base salary. Generous leave options: a standard 29 days (based on a 38 hour working week) per year that you can increase to 41 days by working two hours more per week (flexible working hours). This is prorated if you work part-time. As a TU/e employee, you participate in the ABP pension scheme, providing retirement pension and pension benefits for surviving dependents and occupational disability. TU/e pays 70% of the pension premium, while employees contribute the remaining 30%. A favorable arrangement for more holidays or a sabbatical. A selection model for additional fringe benefits. Working hours in consultation for an optimal work-life balance. Unlimited access to the modern on‑campus TU/e Student Sports Center at an exceptionally affordable rate. We support your wellbeing with free 24/7 access to OpenUp, providing you and your family with mental health support, expert guidance, and online training. Scope for your talent with advancement prospects and excellent development opportunities such as mentoring, workshops and coaching. Partially paid parental leave and reimbursement for commuting expenses, working from home and the internet. On our website you can discover even more information about our conditions of employment . Build on your career at TU/e! About us We are a leading international university where scientific curiosity meets a hands-on mindset. We work in an open and collaborative way with high-tech industries to tackle complex societal challenges. Our responsible and respectful approach ensures impact — today and in the future. TU/e is home to over 13,000 students and more than 7,000 staff, forming a diverse and vibrant academic community. Our university is located in Brainport Eindhoven — a world‑leading tech region with more than 7,000 high‑tech companies and strong R&D activity. Known for breakthroughs in AI, photonics, semiconductors and advanced manufacturing, Brainport is a place where technology serves people and society. Learn more about the Brainport region here . As one of the largest and most dynamic academic communities in the Netherlands, the department Mathematics and Computer Science (M&CS) brings together more than 140 scientific staff, over 250 PhD and EngD candidates, and more than 3000 students. We collaborate closely with leading industrial partners in the Brainport Eindhoven region and with universities across the globe—creating a uniquely fertile environment for both fundamental breakthroughs and applied innovation. Information Do you recognize yourself in this profile and would you like to have more information about the position, please contact the hiring manager Kimberley Thissen , IT business owner , k.k.a.thissen @ tue.nl of +31 40 247 5922. Visit our website for more information about the application process . You can also contact HR Services, HRServices.MCS@ remove-this. tue.nl . Are you inspired and would like to know more about working at TU/e? Please visit our career page. Application If you are interested, please use the ‘apply’ button to send us your CV and letter of application with your motivation and a description of your qualifications. Ensure that you submit all the requested application documents. We give priority to complete applications. Screening of candidates begins as soon as applications are received and continues until the position is filled. Where applicable, internal candidates will be given priority over external candidates where they are equally suitable. We look forward to receiving your application! Please note You can apply online. We will not process applications sent by email and/or post. A pre-employment screening (e.g. knowledge security check) can be part of the selection procedure. For more information on the knowledge security check, please consult the National Knowledge Security Guidelines . Unfortunately, due to the current closure of the Dutch embassy in Tehran , we are unable to consider applications from candidates residing in Iran at this time, as the required immigration procedures cannot be completed. For further information, please visit our FAQ page. Important for non-EU applicants: Please be aware that for this position, specific residence permit requirements apply. If you are a non-EU national, you may not be eligible to legally work in this role under current Dutch immigration regulations. We strongly advise you to contact our Staff Immigration Team ( staffimmigration@tue.nl ) before applying to check your eligibility and to receive further guidance. Please do not contact us for unsolicited services. Reference number: 2026/484 Apply now Share this vacancy Share Twitter Facebook LinkedIn Related vacancies Linux Engineer Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: IT Organisation: Library and Information Services Apply no later than: 18-09-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 3.706 - € 6.682 Read more Senior IAM Engineer Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: IT Organisation: Library and Information Services Apply no later than: 05-09-2026 Full-time equivalent: 0.8 - 1.0 FTE Salary: € 4.925 - € 6.682 Read more Project Manager IT Personal type: Professional staff Field of expertise: IT Organisation: Library and Information Services Apply no later than: 25-09-2026 Full-time equivalent: 1.0 FTE Salary: € 5.932 - € 7.573 Read more Why join TU/e? Join the Eindhoven University of Technology and its thriving community of scientists, students, and professionals. Shape your own career as you become part of a personal university with a big impact. A university where students and lecturers know each other on a first-name basis and work together on innovative projects with real-life significance. Why TU/e? Excellent fundamental research combined with a hands-on mentality Explore our research State-of-the-art research labs Explore our labs World-leading university in cooperation with industry Explore our ecosystem Bachelor programs Master programs Admission and enrollment Working at TU/e Search staff Route & m